1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,387
About 1 in 2 women over 50 will break a bone from bone loss they never even felt coming - here's what's speeding it up.

2
00:00:05,707 --> 00:00:06,940
Soda is the biggest one.

3
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:13,890
Phosphoric acid in cola pulls calcium out of your body - one study found regular cola drinkers had close to 4% lower hip bone density.

4
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:16,743
Swap it for sparkling water or a calcium-fortified drink.

5
00:00:17,063 --> 00:00:20,462
Coffee flushes calcium out through urine, especially once you're past 4 cups a day.

6
00:00:20,782 --> 00:00:23,403
Cap it around 2 to 3 cups, with a splash of milk.

7
00:00:23,723 --> 00:00:31,220
And heavy drinking - more than 2 drinks a day - is linked to a 38% higher fracture risk, partly because it blocks your body from activating vitamin D.

8
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:34,195
Build in a few alcohol-free days and get some daily sunlight.

9
00:00:34,515 --> 00:00:37,758
Watch what you're drinking, and pair it with enough calcium to protect your bones.
